  "about": "Step 24.2 (design-steward 7.8.12, 7.8.12a piece 4): the one media-types table. A file's type is decided by its first bytes (the signatures below, in this order), never by a name or a declared mime; anything else is refused `type`. Read by the steward host's media library (lib/media.mjs) and by the backend (core/media_types.py). limits.call_body_bytes is the steward gateway's request body bound (api/steward_gateway.py MAX_BODY), which media_call checks its base64 against before calling. limits.kept_hours is how long a kept medium lives - a group file sent without mentioning the steward, stored only while that group's switch is on (design/steward-group-media.md section 4): lib/media.mjs stops resolving it and cleans it, and the backend stops listing and deletes its kept_media row. limits.kept_per_group_hour is the kept media's own hourly bound, per group (design/steward-group-media.md section 11): kept rows are not counted in inbound_per_channel_hour, which is the owner's. The pdf_* limits are read_document's (design-steward 7.8.12b, part 6): pages per call with page images and text-only, page images per turn (an owner turn, a group turn), and characters per page and per call. Step 24.2d (7.8.12c \"六\", \"七\"): docx, xlsx and pptx are the rows with `container: \"ooxml\"`; their first bytes are a zip's, which the first-byte signature alone never takes (sniff skips them): the whole file is judged by its zip central directory, read without unzipping anything (ooxmlType: at most office_zip_entries entries and office_unzipped_bytes declared unzipped, no entry past office_zip_ratio compressed 1:N once it declares more than office_zip_ratio_floor bytes, no encrypted entry, no absolute or `..` name, no vbaProject.bin, [Content_Types].xml and exactly one of the three `main_part`s); `container_samples` are the central directories both sides are tested on. The office_* generation limits are make_document's (office_sheet_chars_group: a group turn's xlsx, whose cells, tabs and line breaks the backend's 256 KiB text check must hold at 4 bytes a character), and kept_mimes are the only types a group's un-mentioned file may be kept as (images, voice, PDF). Old OLE office files (doc, xls, ppt and encrypted OOXML), odf, rtf, csv, archives and executables are deliberately absent (v1).",
